package whybotherusingvim

import "naphatsite/web/layouts"

templ Page() {
	@layouts.Base(layouts.MediumContentWidth) {
		<article class="flex flex-col gap-4">
			<header class="mb-4">
				<h1 class="mb-4 font-sans text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">
					Why bother using Vim in the age of AI
				</h1>
				<p class="mb-2">Written by Naphat Amundsen</p>
			</header>
			<p>
				In this day and age during the AI uprising, one may wonder, why care about
				having a good code editor setup?
			</p>
			<p>
				I say, if you still care about having good products, you must at least
				read and understand the central parts. Now that we can generate so
				much code, effective navigation of code and tools is essential.
			</p>
			<p>
				Vim to me, is not just an editor, but a convention. The keybindings of
				Vim is probably the most ubiquitous set of keybindings there are
				related to programming. You can kinda find Vim keybindings seemingly
				everywhere. Like, most code editors have Vim-mode, and a lot developer
				tooling has Vim-like keybindings, you can get Vim-mode in the command
				line. And this to me, is the "superpower" knowing Vim gives you.
			</p>
			<p>
				WIP
			</p>
		</article>
	}
}
